slock - simple screen locker
============================
simple screen locker utility for X.


Requirements
------------
In order to build slock you need the Xlib header files.


Patches
-------
This fork includes the following patches:
    - alpha: adds true transparency to slock.
    - DPMS: turns off the monitor after a configurable amount of time.
    - message (xft): Adds a message to the lock screen with Xft font support.


More
----
Since this build of slock only makes the background transparent, it is intended
to be used with a compositor that is able to provide blur on transparent windows,
like picom for example. Please refer to picom's manual, under the BLUR section, for
more information about how to enable window blurring. Alternatively, a value of 1.0
can be set on config.h for the alpha variable if blur or transparency isn't desired.

Finally, Arch Linux, and Arch-based distributions need user and group set to "nobody",
so it may be required to change the group value to "nogroup" in config.h if one
isn't using any of these distributions.


Installation
------------
Edit config.mk to match your local setup (slock is installed into
the /usr/local namespace by default).

Afterwards enter the following command to build and install slock
(if necessary as root):

    make clean install


Running slock
-------------
Simply invoke the 'slock' command. To get out of it, enter your password.
